# Firestore Realtime Listener

This note is derived from the Firebase snippet set and explains the core idea behind **Firestore Realtime Listener**.

## Why it matters
Subscribe to changes in a collection.

## Example
```firebase
import { collection, onSnapshot } from 'firebase/firestore';
import { db } from './firebaseConfig';

const unsub = onSnapshot(collection(db, "cities"), (doc) => {
    const cities = [];
    doc.forEach((d) => {
        cities.push(d.data());
    });
    console.log("Current cities: ", cities.join(", "));
});

// Call unsub() to stop listening
```

## Review checklist
- Identify the input and output.
- Decide what should be configurable.
- Confirm the naming still matches the domain.
- Add tests or manual checks for failure cases.

